sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, R2-R4, orbit-gateway-renders-create-env (Gateway owns .env), DECISIONS instance.env_import (vault key env-import-<operation_id>, read once, overwritten empty; retire agent command instance.read-environment). docs/reference/environment-variables.md#import.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: env:import
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Instance Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: env:import --instance=42<br/>--replace
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit env:import --instance=42 --replace`
  %%> - syntax: `env:import --instance=SELECTOR [--replace] [--json]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the Instance: a numeric Instance ID or the exact domain of its Route
  %%> - optional `--replace`: file values replace stored keys with the same name
  %%> Who can call it:
  %%> - the `orbit` CLI and the MCP tool send the same request
  %%> When to use it:
  %%> - to adopt the `.env` of a registered checkout, or keys that someone added on the Node
  %%> - this is the one place where environment values come from a Node
  Note over GW: Validate, lock Instance<br/>Instance 42 · task #5132
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12, the Node of Instance 42
  %%> - Instance 42 is active, with complete placement, and Node 12 is active
  %%> - no other task holds Instance 42; the Gateway holds one lock per Instance and waits briefly for a busy one
  %%> Result:
  %%> - task #5132 recorded with the full intent and the `--replace` choice
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-env-import
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  %%> - the account and the `.env` path from the Instance's placement; the caller cannot choose them
  %%> - the vault key to write: `env-import-5132`
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5132
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>N: Check the .env file<br/>@swamp/ssh · owner, type, ≤ 1 MiB
  %%> How:
  %%> - Swamp reaches Node 12 over SSH from 209 with the official `@swamp/ssh` behavior
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks the account, the path, the file type and the owner, without following a link
  %%> - checks the size: at most 1 MiB
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - never reads `.env.example`
  SW->>N: Read .env into the vault<br/>vault.put env-import-5132
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the raw bytes of `.env` and puts them in the vault key `env-import-5132`
  %%> - changes nothing on the Node
  %%> Why the vault:
  %%> - values are secrets; they never enter run inputs, outputs or logs
  %%> Not included:
  %%> - parses nothing; the Gateway owns the import rules
  alt file read and stored
    N-->>SW: bytes, size, sha256
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - to the step only; the bytes go to the vault, not to the run outputs
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>outputs: size, sha256
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    %%> Outputs:
    %%> - the file size and its sha256, no values
    GW->>SW: Read the vault key once<br/>env-import-5132
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - reads the bytes from Swamp's vault on Node 209, once
    %%> Why:
    %%> - this is the only direction change of R3: the values flow Node → vault → Gateway
    Note over GW: Parse, check, store<br/>sha256 · conflicts · APP_KEY
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - checks the sha256 against the run output
    %%> - parses the file as phpdotenv does: quotes, escapes, multiline values, expansion within the file
    %%> - Laravel: stores `APP_URL` as `https://{{instance.domain}}`; an empty `APP_KEY` reuses the stored key or gets a new one
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the keys are stored encrypted; task #5132 succeeds with `changed` and the key count
    %%> - without `--replace`, a key that is already stored stores nothing and fails the task (`env.import_conflict`)
    %%> - a duplicate key or invalid syntax stores nothing (`env.configuration_invalid`)
    %%> Not included:
    %%> - the file on the Node stays the same; run `env:sync` to write it
    GW->>SW: Empty the vault key<br/>env-import-5132 ← empty
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - overwrites the vault key with an empty value, also after a refused import
    %%> Why:
    %%> - Swamp has no vault delete; this is recorded in swamp-evaluation.md
  else missing or unsafe file
    N--xSW: env.import_source_missing
    %%> When:
    %%> - the file is missing, a link, owned by another user, or over 1 MiB
    %%> - SSH fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, no values
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Store nothing<br/>task failed · rerun is safe
    %%> Result:
    %%> - stored configuration stays as it was
    %%> - task #5132 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - nothing changed
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - fix or restore the file, then run `env:import` again; it is a new task
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5132
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
